WEBVTT

00:43.668 --> 00:48.506
DOONA!

01:54.823 --> 01:55.824
Let's go inside.

02:44.622 --> 02:49.002
EPISODE 6

02:49.544 --> 02:50.503
Ha!

02:53.256 --> 02:54.424
All right. Mmm.

03:26.331 --> 03:28.374
Ah! Thank you!

03:28.875 --> 03:30.960
Thank you so much!

03:31.961 --> 03:32.962
Ah.

03:37.050 --> 03:38.426
Ah, wow.

03:38.509 --> 03:42.305
That was an amazing spar between us, huh?
I totally needed that workout.

03:42.388 --> 03:43.223
Hmm.

03:45.225 --> 03:47.435
- So how long have you been doing that?
- Jujitsu?

03:47.936 --> 03:49.520
That was my first session here.

03:50.063 --> 03:52.023
Mmm. You're pretty good, then.

03:52.106 --> 03:54.734
Hey, a few pointers.
Don't rely on your weight, okay?

03:54.817 --> 03:57.946
It's a matter of technique, not just using
your weight as your strength, you know?

03:58.029 --> 03:59.989
How do you beat a natural talent, right?

04:00.073 --> 04:01.115
You just can't.

04:01.616 --> 04:03.993
So, hey, don't get discouraged about this.
Just man up.

04:04.077 --> 04:05.912
Don't worry at all.
You're amazing at yoga.

04:05.995 --> 04:08.957
I've already seen how flexible you can be.

04:09.040 --> 04:11.000
So are you gonna train at that club now?

04:11.084 --> 04:12.293
Yes. Why wouldn't I?

04:13.378 --> 04:14.796
I have to keep getting better

04:14.879 --> 04:17.382
because I want to beat up
my asshole ex-boyfriend, all right?

04:20.510 --> 04:21.469
What's wrong?

04:22.303 --> 04:24.389
Why bother with an asshole
who cheated on you?

04:24.472 --> 04:25.390
Learn to move on.

04:26.391 --> 04:28.101
You can't fix someone like that.

04:28.184 --> 04:30.478
If they've hurt you once before,
they'll do it again.

04:34.315 --> 04:38.027
Well, actually, if you really wanna know
I don't want to fix him at all, okay?

04:38.111 --> 04:39.988
I appreciate it.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.572
I understand.

04:43.074 --> 04:44.325
Jeong-hun.

04:44.409 --> 04:47.036
Thanks for the advice!

04:47.120 --> 04:50.164
DREAM SWEET TO RETURN
AS FOUR-PERSON GROUP WITHOUT DOONA

04:55.712 --> 04:58.089
What could be more interesting
than your best friend, Won-jun?

04:58.172 --> 04:59.090
Your girlfriend?

04:59.173 --> 05:01.759
My Dream Sweet girls
are finally making their comeback.

05:01.843 --> 05:02.885
I'm so excited.

05:03.636 --> 05:06.639
Headlines are popping up,
so I was looking. I'm sorry.

05:06.723 --> 05:09.267
Is that other girl member,
Lee Doona, gonna be a part of it?

05:09.350 --> 05:11.269
I don't know. Just gotta wait and see.

05:11.894 --> 05:14.439
So, um, how's school been going, huh?

05:15.273 --> 05:16.649
Jin-ju, what's going on with her?

05:18.276 --> 05:20.028
So, uh, what kind of person is Lee Doona?

05:21.195 --> 05:22.155
Huh?

05:31.456 --> 05:33.958
LEE DOONA
LEE DOONA WITHDRAWAL, MOM'S DEBT

05:36.252 --> 05:39.672
IDOL DOONA'S PUBLIC IMAGE TAKES A HIT
AS HER MOM'S 700 MILLION DEBT REVEALED

05:42.050 --> 05:43.885
ONLINE FORUM FLOODED WITH POSTERS

05:43.968 --> 05:46.804
CLAIMING TO HAVE BEEN DEFRAUDED
BY DOONA'S MOTHER

05:50.141 --> 05:55.646
LEE DOONA'S MOM ALLEGED TO HAVE DEFRAUDED
VICTIMS OF OVER A BILLION WON

05:59.359 --> 06:01.027
DOONA'S PAINFUL PAST UNCOVERED

06:01.110 --> 06:03.529
RAISED BY GRANDMA FOLLOWING MOM'S DIVORCE

06:43.486 --> 06:44.695
Hey, guess who.

06:45.947 --> 06:47.073
Where are you?

06:47.740 --> 06:49.283
Outside a paper shop.

06:51.744 --> 06:52.829
You sound drunk.

06:53.538 --> 06:54.914
When I was little,

06:55.498 --> 06:56.791
my dad ran a paper shop.

06:56.874 --> 06:58.126
Do you know what that is?

06:59.460 --> 07:01.796
He sold wallpaper and paper flooring.

07:02.380 --> 07:03.548
He repaired lamps.

07:03.631 --> 07:05.216
He basically did everything.

07:05.883 --> 07:08.928
Back then, there were so many things
I wanted to do with him.

07:10.304 --> 07:12.056
But when my dad passed away,

07:13.224 --> 07:16.018
I lost interest in his work
and in other things.

07:16.727 --> 07:19.355
I didn't know
if I could be happy in my life anymore.

07:20.523 --> 07:22.191
I slowly became invisible

07:22.900 --> 07:25.319
and kept to myself as much as possible.

07:26.237 --> 07:30.450
But eventually, I realized
it wasn't what he would've wanted for me.

07:30.533 --> 07:33.286
I knew if he saw how I was living,
he'd hate it.

07:34.203 --> 07:36.664
If he was still here,
he'd tell me to stay strong.

07:40.418 --> 07:41.669
So…

07:43.880 --> 07:46.299
now I do my best
living life to the fullest.

07:50.428 --> 07:52.847
So what I'm trying to get at
is that I, um…

07:53.681 --> 07:55.141
I really like you.

07:56.058 --> 07:58.519
And I'm really jealous
of the people you've dated,

07:59.896 --> 08:02.064
so I really want to know all about you.

08:04.775 --> 08:07.320
That's how I really feel inside, Doona.

08:13.034 --> 08:14.702
I shouldn't have said all that.

08:19.457 --> 08:20.458
Uh-uh.

08:21.918 --> 08:22.752
I'm so sorry!

08:23.544 --> 08:24.712
Thank you so much, sir.

08:26.005 --> 08:26.881
Oh.

08:33.763 --> 08:34.972
I wanna see you.

08:35.973 --> 08:36.849
Right now.

09:34.156 --> 09:35.658
You're actually here.

09:37.118 --> 09:38.578
I was hoping you'd come.

09:40.454 --> 09:42.248
Go back to sleep, okay?

10:50.232 --> 10:51.067
Ta-da!

10:51.150 --> 10:54.320
Whoa, sandwiches!
Whoa, why did you make so many?

10:54.403 --> 10:56.864
The bread was gonna go bad,
so I used it all.

10:56.947 --> 10:59.200
- Yeah, we brought them up to share.
- Ah, I see.

10:59.283 --> 11:00.409
Mm-hmm.

11:01.077 --> 11:02.578
- Thank you.
- Where's Doona at?

11:02.662 --> 11:05.206
Uh, so it looked like she
was still resting in her room,

11:05.289 --> 11:06.916
and we didn't want to wake her up.

11:16.801 --> 11:17.677
Hmm?

11:29.188 --> 11:30.439
So what's this?

11:31.440 --> 11:32.566
Wait a minute.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.403
So are you guys sleeping with each other?
Are you're dating Doona?

11:39.031 --> 11:40.950
Well, so I really like her.

11:41.909 --> 11:42.827
I like her a lot.

11:56.632 --> 11:59.218
So I wonder how long
has this been going on, you know?

11:59.301 --> 12:02.346
She walked out of his room casually,
like it was old news, and we had no idea.

12:02.430 --> 12:04.432
Wow, what a traitor he is.

12:04.515 --> 12:05.933
I know. For real. Ugh.

12:06.016 --> 12:09.395
I once asked him
if they were dating before too, hmm.

12:09.478 --> 12:12.022
"So I really like her."
What?! Dude, what is that?

12:12.773 --> 12:16.235
So they're sleeping together
but not dating, so it's more casual.

12:16.318 --> 12:19.280
So I think it's kind of hip,
don't you agree?

12:19.363 --> 12:21.198
Like on those TV shows.

12:21.282 --> 12:23.659
No, that's not Won-jun's kind of thing.

12:29.039 --> 12:30.541
So, what do you think of all this?

12:30.624 --> 12:33.502
Do you think they are dating
or just sleeping with each other, hmm?

12:33.586 --> 12:36.046
My opinion is it's a violation
of the rules of the house.

12:36.130 --> 12:37.840
I should've said something.

12:38.716 --> 12:40.134
Man, you're no fun at all.

12:43.345 --> 12:45.306
- How do live with that guy?
- That guy?

12:45.389 --> 12:47.850
He's a pretty big jerk.
I told you. I'm sick of him.

13:04.992 --> 13:05.868
You gained weight.

13:15.127 --> 13:16.921
Does your stylist live with you?

13:19.799 --> 13:21.425
No, just a couple friends.

13:21.509 --> 13:22.843
You?

13:22.927 --> 13:24.678
Since when do you have friends?

13:25.638 --> 13:26.514
I do now.

13:27.723 --> 13:28.766
Why are you here?

13:29.850 --> 13:32.603
I heard the other girl members
are returning soon.

13:32.686 --> 13:34.522
Are you going to sit and do nothing?

13:35.105 --> 13:36.440
Why? Are you worried?

13:36.941 --> 13:38.609
You should get what you're owed.

13:39.109 --> 13:40.528
There's money left right?

13:40.611 --> 13:42.238
I'm not owed anything.

13:42.321 --> 13:44.782
I got it all,
then gave everything I had to you.

13:45.282 --> 13:47.952
I'm not even sure how much that was,
because you lost it all.

13:50.371 --> 13:52.206
Well, that's more reason to go back

13:52.289 --> 13:53.707
and beg the girls.

13:56.460 --> 13:59.672
Mom, do you have any idea
why I might've quit?

13:59.755 --> 14:01.465
Aren't you curious to know?

14:01.549 --> 14:03.509
No, because I already know how you are.

14:05.052 --> 14:08.556
You have no work ethic at all.
You have a shit temper, Doona.

14:08.639 --> 14:10.474
And you constantly
turn people against you.

14:23.487 --> 14:25.906
- Is Alice sick?
- I'm sorry, sir?

14:25.990 --> 14:28.701
Jin-ju, she called out of work
today. She didn't tell you?

14:29.201 --> 14:30.035
Oh.

14:30.953 --> 14:32.663
Right. No, she didn't.

14:32.746 --> 14:35.457
I hope she's all right.
This is not like her.

14:42.673 --> 14:44.633
- Hello, welcome.
- Hello.

15:05.821 --> 15:08.824
10 YEARS LATER GROUND

15:22.171 --> 15:23.714
KIM JIN-JU

15:32.222 --> 15:33.223
Uh, hello?

15:35.768 --> 15:36.602
Sorry.

15:37.478 --> 15:39.396
Today must've been tough on your own.

15:40.147 --> 15:42.524
Um, no, it was actually kind of slow.

15:43.484 --> 15:46.070
I heard that there are
supposed to be fireworks tonight.

15:46.153 --> 15:49.198
- Hey, Jin-ju, I, uh…
- Wanna watch them with me?

15:51.200 --> 15:52.493
Just come with me.

15:53.410 --> 15:54.787
I have something to tell you.

15:57.289 --> 15:58.374
Please just come.

16:06.924 --> 16:09.343
Ugh, fireworks?
What are we, children? Seriously.

16:10.135 --> 16:12.680
Hey, shut up.
It's about to start soon, okay?

16:12.763 --> 16:15.766
Anyways, for your information,
I have melancholic depression.

16:16.266 --> 16:17.518
Melancholic depression? Why?

16:17.601 --> 16:20.646
The guy that I hope to date
has no interest in me whatsoever.

16:20.729 --> 16:22.731
- Or so I think.
- Oh, really?

16:22.815 --> 16:24.942
Wait, who is this guy?

16:25.609 --> 16:27.695
- Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh! They're starting!
- Oh! Oh man!

16:27.778 --> 16:29.822
- Oh, look! Look!
- They're starting now!

16:29.905 --> 16:31.699
Oh wow, that was a really big one.

16:49.091 --> 16:50.551
That guy you mentioned…

16:51.552 --> 16:54.722
Not that I know who you're talking about.
I don't know who this person might be.

16:55.389 --> 16:58.350
It's just, well, I think maybe
something traumatic occurred,

16:58.434 --> 16:59.810
like, you know, with other girls.

16:59.893 --> 17:02.021
So what if he lacks confidence now
because of that, huh?

17:04.481 --> 17:07.901
But I don't care about that.
I already think he's super cool.

17:09.445 --> 17:11.447
- Oh.
- Oh! Aw.

17:13.282 --> 17:14.742
Mmm.

17:15.325 --> 17:17.202
- Mmm!
- Oh! That was pretty.

17:17.286 --> 17:18.662
So pretty.

17:18.746 --> 17:20.664
Oh! Man, what a show!

17:21.248 --> 17:22.583
Look, it's a heart! See?

17:28.756 --> 17:31.008
Wow!

17:56.784 --> 17:58.160
Wow, it already started.

17:59.119 --> 18:00.913
Isn't this
why you invited me out?

18:01.413 --> 18:02.998
Yes, sorry.

18:03.665 --> 18:06.335
I asked you to come,
and I was the one that was late.

18:07.503 --> 18:09.546
Well, let's enjoy it before it ends.

18:21.809 --> 18:22.810
Won-jun,

18:24.144 --> 18:26.230
I'm going to tell you something important,

18:26.730 --> 18:30.067
so don't look at me
and just watch the fireworks. Understand?

18:36.615 --> 18:37.991
I like you, Won-jun.

18:41.537 --> 18:44.123
I told you not to look.

18:44.206 --> 18:47.751
- I need you to look at the fireworks.
- Oh, uh…

18:47.835 --> 18:50.963
Since the first time we met,
I've always liked you, okay?

18:52.214 --> 18:54.800
Ever since you helped me
with math in school.

18:55.384 --> 18:56.844
It's kind of funny, right?

18:59.596 --> 19:01.723
1ST PLACE YANGJIN HIGH SCHOOL LEE WON-JUN

19:09.439 --> 19:10.941
LEE WON-JUN

19:44.975 --> 19:46.143
Excuse me.

19:46.810 --> 19:47.644
Oh.

19:49.313 --> 19:51.732
So I heard you're good with math.
Is that right?

19:52.316 --> 19:54.109
Do you think you could help me with this?

19:58.906 --> 19:59.823
Uh…

20:02.326 --> 20:05.454
In the inscribed quadrilateral A-B-C-D
shown in the diagram,

20:05.537 --> 20:08.832
find the length of side B-C
when side A-B is equal to…

20:08.916 --> 20:10.083
Oh.

20:11.084 --> 20:12.085
Use this one.

20:13.295 --> 20:15.464
So the triangle…

20:22.137 --> 20:24.890
Oh, I'm sorry. I gotta leave.

20:26.725 --> 20:29.019
Is it okay if I come to you
for more help later?

20:29.102 --> 20:30.520
Uh, yes, of course.

20:30.604 --> 20:33.398
OSEONG ACADEMY

20:34.441 --> 20:37.319
At a time when there was
so much going on in my life,

20:38.695 --> 20:41.281
talking to you
honestly felt like a breath of fresh air.

20:41.365 --> 20:42.824
Rock, paper, scissors, go!

20:43.325 --> 20:45.744
And every day,
when we'd walk home together…

20:48.830 --> 20:51.792
…I would wish my house
was just a little farther away.

20:53.460 --> 20:56.296
My mind would always
be full of sweet thoughts like that.

20:56.964 --> 21:01.134
I would get butterflies in my stomach
every time I was around you,

21:01.218 --> 21:02.302
and my heart would flutter.

21:05.097 --> 21:07.599
Three. Two. One.

21:14.189 --> 21:16.400
I felt like
we were one and the same.

21:17.234 --> 21:19.945
I like that. Soulmates, huh?

21:20.028 --> 21:21.571
I couldn't tell you how I felt

21:21.655 --> 21:24.157
because I was scared
things might get awkward between us.

21:28.745 --> 21:30.998
I was worried
it would ruin our friendship.

21:35.544 --> 21:37.045
OKAY, TAKE CARE

21:38.839 --> 21:42.092
I didn't have the courage
to tell you what was going on in my life.

21:52.269 --> 21:53.937
I know you've moved on already,

21:55.939 --> 21:58.317
I just want you to know,
or else I'll regret it.

22:00.360 --> 22:01.778
I really like you.

22:02.863 --> 22:06.950
I… I have always liked you
ever since I first laid eyes on you.

22:09.286 --> 22:11.121
And I still feel the same way now.

23:27.155 --> 23:28.281
I've waited so long…

23:30.951 --> 23:32.911
to hear those words from you, you know.

23:33.745 --> 23:36.123
Ever since we became close,
I've always wanted this for us.

23:36.706 --> 23:37.874
I'm sorry that

23:38.542 --> 23:40.460
I was too young then to understand.

23:41.503 --> 23:43.547
I'm really sorry for always hesitating.

23:46.091 --> 23:47.008
And, uh,

23:48.260 --> 23:49.845
for not feeling the same way you do.

23:55.559 --> 23:57.978
Well, then I just hope
that Doona won't break your heart.

23:58.061 --> 24:01.440
And even if she hurts you
and you're full of regret,

24:01.523 --> 24:02.858
I won't take you back.

24:02.941 --> 24:05.485
Lots of boys really like me, Won-jun.
You know that?

24:06.820 --> 24:07.821
I know that.

24:09.030 --> 24:12.117
You're the kind of girl anyone
would be lucky to have, Jin-ju.

24:14.661 --> 24:15.787
So now on,

24:16.580 --> 24:18.915
don't let anyone hurt you anymore.

24:20.584 --> 24:21.918
Not even your family,

24:22.544 --> 24:24.296
'cause you deserve better.

24:27.007 --> 24:29.426
And I'd like to say I'm glad

24:30.093 --> 24:32.179
you're standing up for yourself more now.

24:32.679 --> 24:33.805
It's wonderful.

24:33.889 --> 24:35.432
Don't change that.

25:02.834 --> 25:04.336
It's all over.

25:12.511 --> 25:14.930
You came
to the showcase today, didn't you?

25:35.784 --> 25:37.661
The number
you're trying to reach

25:37.744 --> 25:38.870
is currently unavailable.

25:38.954 --> 25:39.871
LEE DOONA

25:39.955 --> 25:40.956
Please try again later.

25:41.039 --> 25:43.291
RECENTS

25:43.375 --> 25:44.292
LEE DOONA

25:50.215 --> 25:52.342
What are you doing?
It's the middle of the night.

25:54.761 --> 25:57.222
Nothing, really. What about you?

25:57.305 --> 26:00.183
Well, since you asked, I'm taking a walk
because I couldn't sleep.

26:00.267 --> 26:01.643
Then I saw you over here.

26:02.978 --> 26:04.604
You should go back inside.

26:06.189 --> 26:07.107
Hmm.

26:08.692 --> 26:09.526
Hey.

26:10.652 --> 26:13.113
So Jin-ju… she moved out.

26:13.780 --> 26:15.323
She moved to a studio.

26:16.324 --> 26:17.284
I know.

26:18.034 --> 26:19.703
It's all because of you, huh?

26:25.375 --> 26:27.794
Where's Doona? Why isn't she back yet?

26:28.420 --> 26:29.963
I have no idea.

26:31.464 --> 26:34.259
She's your girlfriend.
You ought to know where she is.

26:35.760 --> 26:36.886
Girlfriend, huh?

26:40.265 --> 26:41.266
Is she not?

26:42.934 --> 26:43.852
Oh!

26:44.728 --> 26:47.272
Oh, you bonehead. Ugh.

26:51.610 --> 26:52.444
Hey!

26:54.070 --> 26:55.238
Sit here.

26:56.615 --> 26:58.325
Come, sit. Hurry!

27:08.585 --> 27:09.502
Lee Won-Jun.

27:10.170 --> 27:13.298
Do you know why couples
always celebrate things

27:13.381 --> 27:15.592
like anniversaries or romantic holidays?

27:15.675 --> 27:17.677
Because relationships are contracts.

27:18.178 --> 27:20.305
So it's normal to want to put
some kind of label on it.

27:20.889 --> 27:22.265
But in my experience,

27:22.849 --> 27:25.060
listening to your instincts
can help you a lot.

27:25.644 --> 27:27.354
There's got to be a reason
she won't commit.

27:27.437 --> 27:29.689
She's a celebrity after all.

27:32.692 --> 27:34.194
02:01 A.M.
SUNDAY, SEPTEMBER 17

27:39.658 --> 27:41.910
Don't give away
more than you're getting back, all right?

27:51.044 --> 27:51.920
How about a hug?

27:53.213 --> 27:54.339
No, thank you.

27:55.965 --> 27:56.841
Mmm.

27:57.717 --> 27:58.802
Okay, then.

28:02.097 --> 28:03.807
You got this! I know you do!

28:03.890 --> 28:05.850
Well, um… I'll go for now.

28:06.351 --> 28:07.352
Good night.

28:08.895 --> 28:09.729
All right.

28:15.068 --> 28:16.820
Last chance for that hug…

28:16.903 --> 28:17.737
Hmm.

28:26.246 --> 28:28.081
Well, it's your loss.

28:39.968 --> 28:41.678
LEE DOONA

28:41.761 --> 28:43.346
Oh, hey. Where are you?

29:18.715 --> 29:21.593
Hey,
don't touch that cat. It's filthy.

29:28.683 --> 29:32.228
Hello? Are you here?
Yes, I'll be right out.

29:32.312 --> 29:33.938
No, I'm coming. Just give me a second.

29:34.022 --> 29:35.023
Okay Bye.

29:42.947 --> 29:43.865
Doona.

29:46.576 --> 29:47.911
Why are you sitting here alone?

29:49.454 --> 29:50.789
Let's go on vacation together.

29:50.872 --> 29:52.999
- What?
- You don't wanna go?

29:53.708 --> 29:56.085
Uh, that's not it. Of course I do.

29:56.169 --> 29:57.295
Then let's go now.

30:39.838 --> 30:41.089
Woo-hoo!

30:41.673 --> 30:43.132
Hurry! Come on!

30:44.342 --> 30:45.510
Yay!

30:54.644 --> 30:55.603
It's Won-jun, isn't it?

30:56.855 --> 30:58.147
Huh? Ah.

30:58.231 --> 30:59.566
Won-jun.

31:00.149 --> 31:02.652
Well, that's a possibility.
Statistically speaking, yes.

31:03.236 --> 31:04.863
Okay, but look.

31:05.947 --> 31:07.782
You know I'm a psychology major, right?

31:07.866 --> 31:09.659
And when I start to

31:10.159 --> 31:12.579
really analyze
the multiple non-verbal signs

31:12.662 --> 31:14.080
that she keeps on giving me…

31:17.959 --> 31:19.168
I think I'm the guy.

31:19.252 --> 31:20.128
Don't you think?

31:28.553 --> 31:30.471
Man, I hope
it doesn't get awkward in here.

31:30.555 --> 31:32.849
You know, with all of us living here
under the same roof?

31:35.143 --> 31:37.020
Choi I-Ra.

31:42.692 --> 31:44.652
- Whoo!
- Woo-hoo!

31:45.194 --> 31:46.279
Whoo!

31:46.779 --> 31:47.989
Yeah!

31:50.158 --> 31:51.451
Yay!

31:56.623 --> 31:58.333
Ah, this is so nice.

32:04.589 --> 32:06.341
Jeez! Hurry!

32:08.301 --> 32:09.886
- They're gonna kill us.
- Ah.

32:10.470 --> 32:12.388
Ah! Just ditch it here! Let's go!

32:16.059 --> 32:19.437
- Ah, it's cold. It's cold.
- This is crazy. Isn't it?

32:20.897 --> 32:21.898
Oh. Ah.

32:22.523 --> 32:24.400
Doona, can I have another towel?

32:28.279 --> 32:29.113
Oh.

32:31.157 --> 32:33.493
Hey, hey,
can you help me with this?

32:34.369 --> 32:35.578
Hurry. Hurry.

32:36.704 --> 32:37.830
Take it off. I'm cold.

32:39.749 --> 32:40.917
Hurry.

37:32.375 --> 37:34.919
Jeong-hun! Jeong-hun!

37:35.002 --> 37:36.170
Oh! Hey!

37:36.254 --> 37:38.214
Wait. No, wait! Where are you going?

37:38.297 --> 37:40.633
We have to train together.
What, are you scared to lose?

37:41.467 --> 37:42.468
Bring it on, hmm?

37:44.470 --> 37:45.304
Hmm?

38:12.957 --> 38:14.583
Train somewhere else, okay?

38:24.427 --> 38:25.678
Jeong-hun, wait!

38:26.345 --> 38:28.931
Let's go eat. It's my treat.
Let's go together, yeah?

38:30.141 --> 38:31.642
Oh, come on. Let's go, Jeong-hun.

38:31.726 --> 38:34.353
No, wait. Let's order beef intestines.
It's on me. I'm treating you.

38:34.437 --> 38:36.022
- Ah, jeez.
- Hey, slow down, will you?

38:36.105 --> 38:39.025
Ugh, why did Won-jun have to be
friends with such a crazy girl? Seriously.

38:39.108 --> 38:41.068
I have something I want to say! Wait! Hey!

38:50.786 --> 38:51.829
Oh, what now?

39:09.680 --> 39:11.307
Hey, let's get out of here.

39:12.016 --> 39:14.769
Come on.
Let's go get those beef intestines, hmm?

39:17.646 --> 39:18.564
Ah.

39:20.983 --> 39:23.944
At this point, I don't have
any feelings for him at all.

39:24.028 --> 39:27.114
But seeing him with someone else
really makes me want to snap his neck.

39:29.825 --> 39:32.745
We were together ever since we were kids.
That's eight years in total.

39:33.662 --> 39:35.373
That's eight years
I've wasted on that loser.

39:35.456 --> 39:37.166
Those years won't be returned to you.

39:38.292 --> 39:40.711
But you should try to get
the money he owes, if possible.

39:40.795 --> 39:43.214
Ugh. This really sucks.

39:46.842 --> 39:47.676
Ah.

39:47.760 --> 39:50.971
I don't get people like you and Yun-taek.
You always fall in love, but

39:51.722 --> 39:54.558
you keep on chasing relationships
despite always getting hurt.

39:54.642 --> 39:56.018
Why not avoid all that?

39:57.019 --> 39:58.437
Well, um, you just don't understand.

39:58.521 --> 40:01.148
You don't choose someone to like.
It just happens to you.

40:01.232 --> 40:03.359
Kind of out of the blue
when you least expect it.

40:05.111 --> 40:06.570
You're right. I don't understand it.

40:06.654 --> 40:08.614
Yeah, well, I'm sure one day you will.

40:08.697 --> 40:09.865
Just wait and see, huh?

40:12.910 --> 40:13.911
Hmm.

40:13.994 --> 40:15.454
Go ahead. This is all ready.

40:16.122 --> 40:17.665
I have no appetite.

40:18.541 --> 40:20.418
You still should eat. Have some.

40:25.881 --> 40:26.715
Mmm!

40:26.799 --> 40:28.384
This place is great!

40:28.467 --> 40:30.469
What amazing food, right? Mmm!

40:30.553 --> 40:32.054
Here. Here. Mmm.

40:32.138 --> 40:33.222
Cheers!

40:36.100 --> 40:36.976
Ah!

40:37.476 --> 40:41.188
Mmm, this is so good!
I love it! I'm serious!

40:41.272 --> 40:43.732
Oh, lettuce! Mmm.

40:43.816 --> 40:46.277
I need some more lettuce
with this next one.

40:47.403 --> 40:49.905
- Why aren't you eating?
- I am. Look I'm eating. See?

40:49.989 --> 40:51.949
Mmm! Wow.

40:52.450 --> 40:56.454
The second bite was even better! Mmm!
This place is awesome! Insanely good!

40:56.537 --> 40:57.621
Sorry, what?

40:57.705 --> 40:59.665
- What are you saying right now?
- So good!

40:59.748 --> 41:01.250
Okay, slow down. Chew your food slowly.

41:01.333 --> 41:03.794
Do you even understand
how good this lettuce wrap tastes?

41:16.849 --> 41:18.267
So when do we head back?

41:19.351 --> 41:21.812
Why? You wanna go home or something?

41:21.896 --> 41:24.106
Of course not.
I would much rather stay here.

41:25.024 --> 41:27.276
I actually wanna live here
with you one day.

41:29.695 --> 41:32.031
You actually want something for a change.

41:32.573 --> 41:33.782
I like hearing you say it.

41:38.162 --> 41:39.830
So should we start dating for real?

41:40.831 --> 41:41.790
Like, go public, huh?

41:42.374 --> 41:43.501
Hmm…

41:46.504 --> 41:48.589
What? You look so worried.

41:48.672 --> 41:49.840
It's just, um,

41:51.133 --> 41:52.051
I can't wait!

41:56.388 --> 41:58.224
What should we make for dinner?

43:16.844 --> 43:20.639
MSA HEAD OF TALENT RECRUITMENT
PARK IN-WOOK

43:25.519 --> 43:27.563
Hi. I want to be an idol.
